 if front:
  block=[p('Chandranil Das (261340004) · Devkinandan Sharma (261340005)',ParagraphStyle('authors',parent=style,alignment=1,fontSize=10)),p('Kotak School of Sustainability<br/>M.Tech in AI for Sustainability<br/>Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur · 14 November 2026',ParagraphStyle('aff',parent=style,alignment=1)),sub('Abstract'),p('We implement and verify the real, nonconserved Model-A time-dependent Ginzburg-Landau (TDGL) equation in one and two dimensions. Periodic finite differences and forward Euler time stepping reproduce ordering from small random fluctuations and annihilation of an isolated kink-antikink pair. The full 1D random run uses 1024 points and 1,000,000 steps; the 2D run uses a 128 × 128 mesh and 10,000 steps. Validation includes fixed points, interior kink residuals, temporal order, Fourier eigenmodes, consistency of the discrete energy gradient, and full-step energy monitoring. Spatial and temporal orders are approximately 1.989 and 0.999. Independent replay of all three trajectories covers 1,810,000 steps, with no free-energy increase above 10<super>-9</super>. The random runs remain partially ordered at their recorded endpoints. Optional spectra are interpreted as finite-window diagnostics rather than an ensemble scaling result.')]
